            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SweetPho1083"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The addition of the orange bitters adds the perfect bridge from gin to vermouth. I make mine with two parts gin, one part vermouth, and use a small eye dropper to add a small amount of the orange bitters ( homemade). I find the addition of the one olive is sufficient salt to offset the bitters! For olive/ orange naysayers Spanish tortas come in olive oil orange and are fantastic!",
            "datePublished": "2023-06-10T23:35:22.981Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
